
# B4 – Donor Eligibility Report

## 1. Objective
To generate a donor eligibility report using dynamically allocated memory.

## 2. Dynamic Memory Allocation
The program uses realloc() to increase the donor list capacity when required.

## 3. Memory Management
- malloc/realloc allocate memory.
- A temporary pointer is used with realloc().
- free() releases allocated memory.
- The program avoids memory leaks.

## 4. Eligibility Report
The program displays donor ID, name, age, blood group and eligibility status.

## 5. Performance
The capacity doubles whenever the array becomes full.

This reduces the frequency of memory reallocations compared with increasing capacity by one each time.

## 6. Conclusion
Dynamic memory allocation allows the donor list to grow as new donor records are added. Proper memory management improves reliability.
